@ 36.3.2.2.6 - Proto-rGyalrongic to Tsa Ku Nao
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Nagano, Yashuiki (1979), “A Historical Study of rGyarong Initials and Prefixes”. Linguistics of the Tibeto-Burman Area 4(2):44 – 68; and Nagano, Yashuiki (1979), “A Historical Study of rGyarong Rhymes”. Linguistics of the Tibeto-Burman Area 5(1):37 – 47
	# Initials:
	∅ > n / _pr
	P > p / r_
	çb > ʂp
	Nb > p.
	d(r) çT > t ʃt
	k {sɡ,çK} Nɡ rK > k. sk mɡ nk
	kj > tʃ.
	z > ts / r_
	C[+ sibilant]w > sj
	(P)ç Nç çl > (b)ɕ np.j ʂl
	ts dz NTS KTS sTS > tʃ ts {ts,m} ɡts sp
	s > ʂ / _n
	Nnj > mɲ
	nj rnj > nj rɲ
	∅ > dz / #_j
	# Finals:
	ut u{k,n} ur > ud uo uɛ
	uj > ue
	om > {on,am}
	a(t) > ɛ / _#
	ap > ɛk
	an > ɿɛ
	ew e ej > ə i ei
	i > e / _m
	i i{t,k} > {ə,iɛ} ə
	iŋ > ʅ
	j > ∅ / i_